📌 Portfolio Title
🦉 Leo: Multi-Agent AI Tutor | CrewAI • Python • Streamlit
📝 Full Description (copy and paste)
🦉 LEO: A TEAM OF AI AGENTS THAT TEACHES, QUIZZES & GIVES FEEDBACK
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

💡 THE PROBLEM
Most "AI tutors" are one chatbot answering questions. They don't plan a lesson, test understanding, or notice when a student is struggling. Learners get explanations, but no practice, no feedback, and no continuity between sessions.

🚀 THE SOLUTION
Leo splits tutoring into 4 specialist AI agents that hand work to each other, like a real teaching team:

🧭 Coordinator  →  Understands the request, picks the topic and level, and asks a clarifying question if the request is vague
📘 Explainer  →  Teaches the concept in plain language with a worked example, adapted to the student's past weak areas
📝 Quiz Master  →  Creates practice questions from the lesson as validated, structured data
✅ Evaluator  →  Grades answers, explains mistakes, and flags weak areas

🔁 If the score is low, weak areas go back to the Explainer for a focused re-teach.
🧑 The student answers the quiz personally (human-in-the-loop), and the live interface shows which agent is working at each step.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

⚙️ WHAT MAKES IT TECHNICALLY CHALLENGING
✔ Real agent-to-agent handoffs using typed Pydantic schemas, not isolated prompts
✔ Sequential orchestration designed to pause for human input mid-pipeline
✔ Persistent per-student memory that changes how later lessons are taught
✔ A dedicated prompt template for each agent role
✔ Retry logic and clarification handling, so a vague request or failed step doesn't crash the session
✔ Provider-agnostic: switch between OpenAI and Anthropic models by changing one setting

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

🎯 WHO NEEDS THIS & WHY IT MATTERS
🏫 EdTech startups: personalized tutoring without hiring a tutor for every subject
🎓 Course creators & coaches: add interactive practice and feedback to existing content
🏢 Corporate training teams: onboarding and compliance learning with built-in assessment
📚 Tutoring centers & schools: explore AI-assisted study tools

💼 BUSINESS VALUE
One-to-one tutoring is expensive and hard to scale. A multi-agent design is more structured and reliable than a single chatbot, and each agent can be improved, replaced, or extended independently (new subjects, new quiz formats, new tools).

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

🛠️ TECH STACK
Python • CrewAI • Pydantic • Streamlit • OpenAI & Anthropic APIs (via LiteLLM) • JSON-based memory • Git/GitHub

